      "extract": "Let $G$ be a semi-simple algebraic group over an algebraically closed characteristic zero field $\\mathsf k$. The fundamental object of the geometric Langlands duality theory is the so-called *Satake category ${Perv_{{\\bf G_O}}(\\Gr)}$*. The latter is defined as the category of perverse sheaves on the affine (loop) Grassmannian $\\Gr$ equivariant with respect to the group of regular loops ${\\bf G_O}$. It turns out that",
